## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/dot.html
- Summary (EN): Computes a per-pixel dot product of two layers and outputs a single mono layer: for each pixel, corresponding channel values are multiplied and summed.
- Résumé (FR) : Calcule le produit scalaire pixel par pixel de deux couches, avec une sortie mono.

- Inputs meaning: ["a: first layer or VDB, the reference for the operation", "b: second layer or VDB, extended with the channel extension rules so its channels match a"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source (linked to the Signatures glossary)"]

- Caveats: ["The channel extension rules are not explained on the page; only a glossary link is given.", "The output is always mono, so multichannel colour is collapsed into one value per pixel."]

